</div>
<p local-id=3D"cebf1d17-c9da-4d7d-8f80-ca50578576f5"><strong>=F0=9F=93=9D I=
mportant Distinction:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"36122541-1e2e-4178-a00e-56ca61329394">
<li local-id=3D"43113d6d-1d3a-41c2-ad54-27105c22b0c8">
<p local-id=3D"6da7c33e-35f3-4362-a658-d455d7f4c9f6"><strong>Developer ID A=
pplication</strong> =3D Sign apps, binaries, frameworks (what you need!)</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"1083007e-4d08-4e96-8065-5d2994996b7a">
<p local-id=3D"534b0a4b-b279-4116-85aa-62ddc88b1bb1"><strong>Developer ID I=
nstaller</strong> =3D Sign .pkg installer packages (you don't need this)</p=
></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"0b00e79d-05a8-425c-8e3b-dc9f651d5320"><strong>Install certif=
icates to Keychain:</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"13d19033-ed26-4745-b2c5-e3baa104652b">First, check what pass=
word to use:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># View =
the password (you'll need it in a moment)
cat password.txt</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"1ccf771e-23eb-4a55-8557-ca0fd31c3934">Now import the certifi=
cates:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Step =
1: Install Apple's intermediate certificate first
security import Apple-Developer-ID-Certification-Authority.cer \
  -k ~/Library/Keychains/login.keychain-db

# Step 2: Install your Developer ID Application certificate
# This will prompt for the password from password.txt
security import Apple-Developer-ID-Application-2025.p12 \
  -k ~/Library/Keychains/login.keychain-db \
  -T /usr/bin/codesign \
  -T /usr/bin/productsign

# When prompted, enter the password from password.txt</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"c58a0c0c-3ff0-43b1-b353-453ace51d850"><strong>Breaking down =
the import command:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"56908008-c0ad-4aa1-af2e-3f15238748d2">
<li local-id=3D"8db6eca2-1a3a-4b2a-8b46-5c6048d2fecb">
<p local-id=3D"2cf0def3-b973-46ed-91fc-3fa37d6af6d9"><code>-k ~/Library/Key=
chains/login.keychain-db</code> - Import to your login keychain</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4f235568-bb35-4f1b-990d-8cbfbbc254ad">
<p local-id=3D"2022a828-ae10-4da7-9e88-f16e7f311cac"><code>-T /usr/bin/code=
sign</code> - Allow codesign to use this without password prompt</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"62fa1786-6254-4ef1-9aeb-1a3ce88a147b">
<p local-id=3D"e932f6ec-ad1d-48c9-ab70-f1bf8174ea98"><code>-T /usr/bin/prod=
uctsign</code> - Allow productsign to use this without password prompt</p><=
/li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"4bd25e95-a79f-48dc-8267-d48ada2d6861"><strong>Note:</strong>=
 You might be prompted for your macOS user password to allow the import.</p=
>
<p local-id=3D"549006fb-c42a-491a-9b21-125087870de4"><strong>Securely store=
 your API key and clean up:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Creat=
e secure directory for API key
mkdir -p ~/.apple-keys
chmod 700 ~/.apple-keys

# Move your .p8 API key to secure location (you received this separately)
# If you have it in Downloads or current directory:
mv ~/Downloads/AuthKey_*.p8 ~/.apple-keys/ 2&gt;/dev/null || echo "Move you=
r .p8 file manually"
chmod 600 ~/.apple-keys/AuthKey_*.p8 2&gt;/dev/null

# IMPORTANT: The .p8 file is NOT in the certificates zip - it's a separate =
file
# Make sure you know where your AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8 file is located

# Clean up ALL certificate files (they're now safely in Keychain)
cd ~
rm -rf ~/tmp/signing-setup

echo "=E2=9C=85 Certificates imported to Keychain and temporary files delet=
ed"
echo "=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F  Make sure your .p8 API key is in ~/.apple-keys/"<=
/pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"6cec6c81-26d7-4ab4-a599-3755f227ece6"><strong>What got clean=
ed up vs. what remains:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"82570f2e-e7b0-4f67-be2f-a63807a699b8">
<li local-id=3D"7b5bb2d8-1673-4712-8413-6adef885c0b8">
<p local-id=3D"a418920a-91b9-4646-a6c5-2d8ac61aa57a">=E2=9C=85 <strong>Dele=
ted:</strong> All <code>.p12</code>, <code>.cer</code>, <code>.pem</code>, =
<code>password.txt</code> files (no longer needed)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c6c61b6b-0317-453b-b4a3-f7a591901509">
<p local-id=3D"76144d24-8512-497a-a59a-6b0434992335">=E2=9C=85 <strong>In K=
eychain:</strong> Your certificates and private keys (secure, encrypted by =
macOS)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"df82310c-3167-4277-b675-13e7a975995c">
<p local-id=3D"cb622f73-2343-4bbe-b99f-8cfe3b472883">=E2=9C=85 <strong>Kept=
:</strong> Your <code>.p8</code> API key file in <code>~/.apple-keys/</code=
> (needed for notarization)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"beca5af1-73f1-4851-b567-be600384462e"><strong>Why delete the=
 certificate files?</strong><br>
They're now securely stored in your macOS Keychain. Leaving them in tempora=
ry directories is a security risk. The Keychain is encrypted and protected =
by your user password.</p>
<p local-id=3D"03cdef31-ed36-4e43-8a8e-7eaef9f1b15f"><strong>Verify certifi=
cates are installed:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">securit=
y find-identity -v -p codesigning</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"4635acb2-b0a0-44ae-8126-0ae5cfa62d5b"><strong>What to look f=
or:</strong> You should see something like:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">1) ABC1=
23DEF456789 "Developer ID Application: BlazeMeter Ltd (TEAM123456)"
     1 valid identities found</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"ded5cf84-d06d-45c0-8053-74ccc5599db7"><strong>Understanding =
the output:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"bb7f2737-5e17-4dbe-aa49-483b34debdbc">
<li local-id=3D"5262dbb6-fdcb-4c4a-afbf-489851dfa123">
<p local-id=3D"bfea5cdf-8896-46a6-8bfb-0914186b53e1"><code>ABC123DEF456789<=
/code> - The certificate's SHA-1 hash (unique identifier)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a6959107-5206-4626-9214-2f266fcfe76d">
<p local-id=3D"d3828078-8ad2-4d13-bf83-167d1d3f2ecd"><code>"Developer ID Ap=
plication: BlazeMeter Ltd (TEAM123456)"</code> - The certificate's common n=
ame</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"904d646d-b10d-4a91-be96-ff1557c94a61">
<p local-id=3D"8a6b23e9-f630-4799-8ae5-ecac20776690">The company name and T=
eam ID will match your Apple Developer account</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"ab31e4d4-b4ae-4fc9-9670-c739eb6c519d"><strong>Save your sign=
ing identity:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># This =
is what you'll use in codesign commands
# Copy the ENTIRE quoted string (including quotes)
SIGNING_IDENTITY=3D"Developer ID Application: BlazeMeter Ltd (TEAM123456)"

# Verify it's set correctly
echo "Your signing identity: $SIGNING_IDENTITY"</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"877b71e6-5647-45dd-808c-56f4f7d7c478"><strong>Optional: Test=
 your signing identity works</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Creat=
e a test file and try signing it
echo "test" &gt; /tmp/test-sign
codesign --sign "$SIGNING_IDENTITY" /tmp/test-sign
codesign --verify --verbose /tmp/test-sign
# Should output: /tmp/test-sign: valid on disk
rm /tmp/test-sign</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"168ea845-a59b-4f03-9720-9856a0351cb0"><strong>If you see "0 =
valid identities found":</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"2f31f620-1179-49ab-b5c3-97b1ef2eec7e">
<li local-id=3D"664aa39d-076d-45d7-908f-09ac005f21cd">
<p local-id=3D"2605ec43-97cd-4f65-bbb7-a0fe4f54c02b">The import failed</p><=
/li>
<li local-id=3D"60097880-5380-4f97-a7ad-bc3803a11807">
<p local-id=3D"54600cab-4f27-4c78-b99f-985da3268f38">You entered the wrong =
password</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"389e8ee2-3a49-4d84-a4e2-750ab15df765">
<p local-id=3D"b810c34e-085c-4041-9b6b-11bf22b4fca0">The certificate is exp=
ired</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"427f1f34-8338-4702-b8c5-6aa00b7f3cde">
<p local-id=3D"b34fc9b8-63d2-444e-aa61-3c217470752f">Try the import steps a=
gain</p></li>
</ul>
<hr local-id=3D"091bd73f-3749-4242-bba1-2e05ce637968">
<h2 local-id=3D"dd21ea68-c3f1-433d-a612-99d6563d6051" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8FPart3:PyInstaller-SpecificRequirement=
s(=E2=8F=B0ONE-TIMESETUP)">=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F Part 3: PyInstaller-Specific =
Requirements (=E2=8F=B0 ONE-TIME SETUP)</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"cb1c1dd6-0570-4b5f-aacd-0d2c0f068714" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step3:UnderstandingPyInstaller+HardenedRuntimeIssues">S=
tep 3: Understanding PyInstaller + Hardened Runtime Issues</h3>
<p local-id=3D"88324a8c-0e5e-473b-aeb5-f0fe6971774e"><strong>CRITICAL FOR P=
YINSTALLER APPS:</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"d7868b4c-8375-43f8-a455-919039b88d44">If you're signing a Py=
Installer binary (like bzm-mcp), you <strong>MUST</strong> use entitlements=
. Without them, your app will fail with a Team ID mismatch error.</p>
<p local-id=3D"17252ac5-e602-49ea-983e-e39e002689b3"><strong>Why this happe=
ns:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"7f5b9c2a-8a98-49d7-ac00-aa9d79020b4a">
<li local-id=3D"41ec8e8d-0ba5-42aa-bdec-685ac0d3d0b9">
<p local-id=3D"0d72714e-433a-4761-8cfe-8ba2e6300f61">PyInstaller bundles Py=
thon.framework inside your binary</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c0bc621d-5963-43a0-92d7-2604c0c27bdc">
<p local-id=3D"84bd0284-8773-45da-a2ea-7a86a3365dba">At runtime, it extract=
s Python to a temporary folder</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a8362264-4c92-4de0-9ef6-8e526962d829">
<p local-id=3D"241e0189-9d85-4a7b-879e-b5cfbdcafcdd">With hardened runtime =
enabled, macOS strictly checks signatures</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a189427a-6c0d-46a0-9993-ffd78f1dc1e4">
<p local-id=3D"fbbeab81-8005-4da8-b8a0-c3b3bcaffcd4">The extracted Python f=
ramework may have a different (or no) Team ID</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"dba54d22-8f65-4080-a385-84e7adeba23a">
<p local-id=3D"c7e6471f-11cb-4966-a83c-8ce0f5343028">macOS blocks it unless=
 you explicitly allow it with entitlements</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"adaf4352-f94f-47e1-8a69-ed6c12fe8ca6" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step4:CreateEntitlementsFile">Step 4: Create Entitlemen=
ts File</h3>
<p local-id=3D"4866541b-c813-474f-a957-2252ff8d882a"><strong>Create the ent=
itlements file in your project:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">cd /Use=
rs/joaquinaraujo/github/bzm-mcp

cat &gt; entitlements.plist &lt;&lt; 'EOF'
&lt;?xml version=3D"1.0" encoding=3D"UTF-8"?&gt;
&lt;!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.c=
om/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd"&gt;
&lt;plist version=3D"1.0"&gt;
&lt;dict&gt;
    &lt;!-- Allow loading libraries not signed with the same Team ID --&gt;
    &lt;!-- Required for PyInstaller's bundled Python framework --&gt;
    &lt;key&gt;com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation&lt;/key&gt;
    &lt;true/&gt;
   =20
    &lt;!-- Allow DYLD environment variables --&gt;
    &lt;!-- Required for PyInstaller's dynamic library loading --&gt;
    &lt;key&gt;com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables&lt;/k=
ey&gt;
    &lt;true/&gt;
   =20
    &lt;!-- Allow unsigned executable memory --&gt;
    &lt;!-- Required for JIT compilation in some Python packages --&gt;
    &lt;key&gt;com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory&lt;/k=
ey&gt;
    &lt;true/&gt;
&lt;/dict&gt;
&lt;/plist&gt;
EOF</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"c008669a-5008-4855-a35b-743da77197f4"><strong>What each enti=
tlement does:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"85=
5d0648-f335-4eb5-97f1-175f87f9e626" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"bfeb405d-bf37-4db9-8027-cafad0b7f802">
<th data-local-id=3D"1195cdb6-0094-4428-8cca-374babde84ca" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"c50cafd1-2f7a-4126-8373-296537cf45cd">Entitlement</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"db5118ec-fb9a-43e3-87fd-f7e4ff168426" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"5be76d60-a480-43f3-b6bf-2d7078dc2749">Purpose</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"61a99a55-03c2-4805-b0b5-bb2e033c2e81" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"72824c17-46e3-45ca-b807-a77c4099f5ce">Why PyInstaller Needs =
It</p></th>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"5d76cc08-609b-4c54-8e13-c6e8007ee0b4">
<td data-local-id=3D"dc64428c-a066-43c1-a04e-6ba6c95e975e" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"d52ca55a-e339-4942-a2cc-6e08d32a1674"><code>disable-library-=
validation</code></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"76afa61a-0fc8-48ca-9ce1-cfc3e6ff8cb2" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"55a027a2-ad8f-4a7b-9012-fffc2ec04740">Allow loading librarie=
s with different Team IDs</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"270a7f7c-1164-4e3e-9bad-7845aa6d687a" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"77a3ffaa-c7ac-4b81-a184-0aba0a2dbe4e">Python.framework has d=
ifferent/no Team ID</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"64e134ec-ee75-4839-aa8d-274037a9227e">
<td data-local-id=3D"3590bb66-1a8d-455c-9611-545807de396e" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"5f1e21a9-00be-48a4-9b2f-29655987a577"><code>allow-dyld-envir=
onment-variables</code></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"5ed115d3-8fb9-4fcd-a3b2-5e3a3980d9ad" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"07113613-2d59-43ed-9b5d-d8dfec932c28">Allow DYLD_* env vars<=
/p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"7cb8cc23-e894-4823-8745-cf9400d21ff5" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"46a0bf8a-80ba-4560-96a2-3eb409b21cda">PyInstaller uses these=
 for library paths</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"f4c2dd0d-bd65-42b3-a6fc-7a7a8d7cb7a8">
<td data-local-id=3D"e48c29fc-0575-4d1a-a9fa-2f0eca847e4f" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"22bc8a35-7a12-49ee-83ac-090ab667e7b9"><code>allow-unsigned-e=
xecutable-memory</code></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"371b2ae9-7aa7-4620-bbce-cd01b1ed4207" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"f59e11d5-8ed1-4f7e-98de-620fad62f474">Allow JIT/dynamic code=
 execution</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"9fd5a77c-b1dd-419c-b1af-bc83887c1b9f" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"ec571beb-364f-43bc-91b1-4134fa095592">Some Python packages (=
numpy, etc.) need this</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"861a48d6-11d2-400d-9a86-98829113b5bb"><strong>Security Note:=
</strong> These entitlements reduce some security restrictions but are <str=
ong>necessary for PyInstaller apps</strong> and <strong>still allow notariz=
ation</strong>. Apple accepts these for legitimate use cases.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6faafc6b-e615-484c-9b6e-a34d774ae004"><strong>Save this file=
 in your repository</strong> - you'll need it for every build!</p>
<hr local-id=3D"a0a9024e-8860-430b-91e4-10309e106376">
<h2 local-id=3D"5bbef2ea-278e-4197-a435-75ab57f07537" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-=F0=9F=93=8BQuickSummary:AfterInitialSetupisComplete">=
=F0=9F=93=8B Quick Summary: After Initial Setup is Complete</h2>
<p local-id=3D"719fa161-b482-4e15-a5a3-9a29a9bb9e4f"><strong>=F0=9F=8E=89 C=
ongratulations!</strong> Once you've completed Parts 1-3 above (ONE-TIME SE=
TUP), you don't need to repeat those steps.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f972fbdd-cfad-4788-80e6-c9f1ddc20274"><strong>What you did o=
nce (never repeat unless credentials expire):</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"d16120e1-63c3-4390-8f3c-6977b606a1bb">
<li local-id=3D"c956fc8e-64d0-4c12-bcea-7a821b4733a6">
<p local-id=3D"bfed87d0-bbb4-4626-9254-b1fbf919bb3d">=E2=9C=85 Installed Xc=
ode Command Line Tools</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2778b406-4f3d-49f0-867a-5440ba2287ee">
<p local-id=3D"09f9a6d9-3a11-447e-bd5f-b8db33d5fecb">=E2=9C=85 Imported cer=
tificates to Keychain</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a2a39a2f-8b03-425e-abf4-e9480689d288">
<p local-id=3D"3f54bec6-7b84-4d3a-a5e6-7b4fb0cafe1c">=E2=9C=85 Stored API k=
ey in <code>~/.apple-keys/</code></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2f47f24c-e683-4bde-af61-c848e5103dfd">
<p local-id=3D"6272eccf-92f3-4242-8ade-6bb668c86d74">=E2=9C=85 Stored notar=
ization credentials with <code>notarytool store-credentials</code></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"52cd5a06-5f82-43b4-977b-19a886a9a28b">
<p local-id=3D"17621704-334e-42d6-9416-3566232d3ec3">=E2=9C=85 Created <cod=
e>entitlements.plist</code> file</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"3351a514-7317-4866-8ea9-1cba05f5af7a"><strong>For every subs=
equent build, you only need to:</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"da642744-c23f-431b-887a-935bfe253f2b"><strong>Common Steps (=
1-4):</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"4e29a3db-313d-42d0-910b-896c7a63e50b">
<li local-id=3D"cfbcab7c-b77f-422a-a538-49dcf6b2ec2e">
<p local-id=3D"f7f9303b-4435-41bc-925b-2ed18d238862"><strong>Build your bin=
ary</strong> (with your normal build process)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"dad60a05-27f0-45d7-b61f-2dccaac0bb47">
<p local-id=3D"f438be26-01a1-483f-bac6-8fb2824d996b"><strong>Check quaranti=
ne</strong> =E2=86=92 <code>xattr -l</code> and remove if present</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e781a941-548f-48cf-910f-396ed79da4b1">
<p local-id=3D"02ffea15-b14f-432b-a98a-58748281f997"><strong>Remove adhoc s=
ignature</strong> =E2=86=92 <code>codesign --remove-signature</code></p></l=
i>
<li local-id=3D"45f17b50-9c3c-465e-836f-d56e886b3b68">
<p local-id=3D"94876a8c-a375-468a-b153-05bdba524b6f"><strong>Sign binary</s=
trong> =E2=86=92 with <code>--entitlements</code> and <code>--options runti=
me</code></p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"85f44b58-b0eb-4ac2-85a1-99f49fb91d29"><strong>ZIP Method (Cu=
rrent - Steps 5-7):</strong><br>
5. <strong>Create ZIP</strong> =E2=86=92 <code>ditto -c -k --sequesterRsrc =
--keepParent</code><br>
6. <strong>Notarize ZIP</strong> =E2=86=92 Submit to Apple (1-5 mins)<br>
7. <strong>Test</strong> =E2=86=92 Verify everything works</p>
<ul local-id=3D"fd77557a-14fe-4343-9514-f71929942af8">
<li local-id=3D"5aa812c6-7947-4ec9-8a9b-938aa712067b">
<p local-id=3D"d0dea69f-7009-4724-b55d-6b5a5444c041">=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F Not=
e: ZIP cannot be stapled, requires internet on first run</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"f76327fd-a5ae-4c8d-9a17-6507dd7fbb99"><strong>DMG Method (Al=
ternative - Steps 5-9):</strong><br>
5. <strong>Create DMG</strong> =E2=86=92 Package signed binary<br>
6. <strong>Sign DMG</strong> =E2=86=92 Sign the DMG container<br>
7. <strong>Notarize DMG</strong> =E2=86=92 Submit to Apple (1-5 mins)<br>
8. <strong>Staple DMG</strong> =E2=86=92 Embed notarization ticket (offline=
 verification)<br>
9. <strong>Test</strong> =E2=86=92 Verify everything works</p>
<p local-id=3D"aeac6711-1722-4077-b42b-3adae896c029"><strong>That's it!</st=
rong> Just follow Parts 4-9 below for each new build. The process becomes q=
uick and straightforward once setup is done.</p>
<hr local-id=3D"60807d9f-1314-4e8d-93c8-2584757b194c">
<h2 local-id=3D"e43ad887-3661-4cec-ba1e-607622570e17" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-=F0=9F=94=90Part4:CodeSigningYourBinary(=F0=9F=94=84EVE=
RYBUILD)">=F0=9F=94=90 Part 4: Code Signing Your Binary (=F0=9F=94=84 EVERY=
 BUILD)</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"7d0ea872-3ee3-42f9-8920-55ae8c999871" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step5:UnderstandWhatSigningDoes">Step 5: Understand Wha=
t Signing Does</h3>
<p local-id=3D"ed1cbcdb-20b2-4732-8c97-9ad255a31288">When you sign a binary=
:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"ca488b60-9788-4607-ae5d-b3633aae8c0b">
<li local-id=3D"0ca43ba6-9a84-4ac2-91ac-cfdd8860c0a4">
<p local-id=3D"1fe2771f-4b40-4e49-87d6-fb012b73a1a9">macOS calculates a cry=
ptographic hash of your binary</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5f5bff70-5d41-4959-9ecd-30d2b16bf50a">
<p local-id=3D"3509683c-a2ae-4381-9ec3-0e782d829971">It encrypts that hash =
with your private key</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7572ad83-7f52-4885-a831-67ee62f50b20">
<p local-id=3D"c19bfd7e-8e41-4816-bc2e-9ede44dcd161">The signature is embed=
ded in the binary</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9f1f91a6-02c1-485b-8620-8a0b6bce36e7">
<p local-id=3D"4a885ac0-fdbb-4631-9419-1a4f26e80377">When a user runs it, m=
acOS verifies the signature matches</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"7baa125e-6dca-461a-80d9-7e9ec3687bc4"><strong>The guarantee:=
</strong> If even one byte changes, the signature becomes invalid.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"fbdbb186-c11b-401f-baa4-7f013228fafb" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step6:CheckandRemoveQuarantineAttribute">Step 6: Check =
and Remove Quarantine Attribute</h3>
<p local-id=3D"4cf0a963-dd4a-441e-87f6-5f6493348203"><strong>CRITICAL:</str=
ong> Before signing, check if the binary has a quarantine attribute. This c=
an cause the signing process to fail or create issues later.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">cd /Use=
rs/joaquinaraujo/github/bzm-mcp/dist

# Check if binary is quarantined
xattr -l bzm-mcp-macos-arm64</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"3b97f92d-0d17-4588-905c-b9d857f5fd8b"><strong>If you see </s=
trong><code>com.apple.quarantine</code> in the output:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Remov=
e the quarantine attribute
xattr -d com.apple.quarantine bzm-mcp-macos-arm64

# Verify it's gone
xattr -l bzm-mcp-macos-arm64</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"2faa2269-5d73-4be9-8266-8be1a31d82b3"><strong>Why this matte=
rs:</strong> macOS marks downloaded files with a quarantine attribute. If y=
our binary has this attribute, it can interfere with code signing and cause=
 security warnings even after proper signing and notarization.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"af0b77f2-b9cd-4311-ab0f-355c5b4f8f75" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step7:RemoveExistingSignatures">Step 7: Remove Existing=
 Signatures</h3>
<p local-id=3D"b601e420-aa44-4724-a672-4cf9c4881e06">PyInstaller automatica=
lly adds an <strong>adhoc signature</strong> (self-signed). You must remove=
 it first:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Remov=
e the adhoc signature
codesign --remove-signature bzm-mcp-macos-arm64</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 local-id=3D"6d0984ca-6fa5-4707-ba72-5f75a34875bf" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step8:SignYourBinary(WITHEntitlements)">Step 8: Sign Yo=
ur Binary (WITH Entitlements)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"2e2f5fb8-ff46-4a95-b20a-ddf34c14f218"><strong>Sign it with y=
our Developer ID and entitlements:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">codesig=
n --sign "Developer ID Application: Your Name (TEAM_ID)" \
  --entitlements ../entitlements.plist \
  --options runtime \
  --timestamp \
  --force \
  --deep \
  --verbose \
  bzm-mcp-macos-arm64</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"1fedeeaa-fdbd-4acb-9c15-e149ece97c52"><strong>Breaking down =
the flags:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"cbbc04bd-6933-4f1c-b846-ee7f8b8e406c">
<li local-id=3D"d88576ff-fbec-4363-a253-690f4348e7b4">
<p local-id=3D"797e5cbd-07e5-4758-b803-c199af70cfea"><code>--sign "..."</co=
de> - Use this specific certificate identity</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ef9af9b9-ef4c-4aa3-8a87-a0e0b7a11b40">
<p local-id=3D"75226512-dcd8-479c-822a-b45381b4bbbd"><code>--entitlements</=
code> - <strong>CRITICAL:</strong> Path to your entitlements file</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"bc586039-2332-48a5-b62e-9feb026012c7">
<p local-id=3D"d0cfc4b8-15f4-498d-9a0c-37c18dc5920f"><code>--options runtim=
e</code> - Enable hardened runtime (required for notarization)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"742cd63c-6304-4835-8650-893575600e2f">
<p local-id=3D"f5ede9b1-7146-4885-97e1-95fc7a0a9628"><code>--timestamp</cod=
e> - Include a trusted timestamp (proves when it was signed)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cc31ab06-3bdc-43cb-83fa-ef23c7b265b0">
<p local-id=3D"3e449b60-0047-4928-a929-87b07c5d538a"><code>--force</code> -=
 Replace any existing signature</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2ad4aaf6-5e98-4bd1-b03a-06a8329b968e">
<p local-id=3D"4c688ef7-5b12-4880-b55e-e94d8505be8a"><code>--verbose</code>=
 - Show what's happening</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"c8e6b351-e6c0-4b28-8c03-602e63cba4c9" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step9:VerifytheSignature">Step 9: Verify the Signature<=
/h3>
<p local-id=3D"3b482565-b893-4f43-8a4f-034c293bd314"><strong>Check the sign=
ature is valid:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">codesig=
n --verify --verbose bzm-mcp-macos-arm64</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"e8a001a0-f52c-46da-b04e-cb527c94a5c8"><strong>Check signatur=
e details:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">codesig=
n --display --verbose=3D4 bzm-mcp-macos-arm64</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"07770854-fdf3-4a14-8732-1ea3b4c0d545"><strong>What to look f=
or:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"514c0a40-baa9-47a6-aee5-c753403ee80a">
<li local-id=3D"5d997c2b-c3e5-4baf-a812-fa67b65fa93f">
<p local-id=3D"6cec3845-5913-4228-bee1-1249710be90f">=E2=9D=8C <code>Signat=
ure=3Dadhoc</code> means NOT properly signed (bad!)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"49b1033a-56c6-4ecf-b0ac-8a11e98015a3">
<p local-id=3D"cab8c99b-a15f-4a98-bb53-947b42a82f1c">=E2=9C=85 <code>Author=
ity=3DDeveloper ID Application: Your Name</code> means properly signed (goo=
d!)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f7eb9755-7c2b-4d42-9176-739d7fee522a">
<p local-id=3D"5eb9a04a-c6d7-407e-a8e4-153d0dd5410a">=E2=9C=85 <code>Timest=
amp=3D...</code> should show a date (good!)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c74b5978-4a7d-47b0-8110-47ef3232351b">
<p local-id=3D"5b5a1d06-5dd4-4bf0-8b44-67abacd16585">=E2=9C=85 <code>Runtim=
e Version=3D...</code> confirms hardened runtime is enabled</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"3d3e8cc0-b05d-433f-ab60-84ceca852b8b"><strong>Verify entitle=
ments were applied:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">codesig=
n --display --entitlements - bzm-mcp-macos-arm64</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"904a07de-68f0-4861-800e-43c5f36e1919">You should see your th=
ree entitlements listed in XML format.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"874637d4-5370-4757-a0c3-3223053aaaed" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step10:TesttheBinaryLocally">Step 10: Test the Binary L=
ocally</h3>
<p local-id=3D"62c5fa30-9789-49a9-96fa-5581a1ad3151"><strong>Before creatin=
g the DMG, test the binary works:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">./bzm-m=
cp-macos-arm64 --version
# or
./bzm-mcp-macos-arm64 --help</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"a1624005-5930-4ee8-b056-dfe55f80529b"><strong>If it fails wi=
th "Team ID" errors:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"b99f3761-d287-4a64-ab05-7ba38f1dec89">
<li local-id=3D"30609ef1-458f-422c-8246-7ad671a59f3c">
<p local-id=3D"22de7e28-8572-4aef-9bf4-9fc3f4115413">The entitlements weren=
't applied correctly</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6a8d1a9a-ed8f-4abe-b288-73c687f618d5">
<p local-id=3D"3a29ec86-080d-4d92-8cb2-ebf62b20d36a">Re-check the <code>--e=
ntitlements</code> path</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"31d4e6f7-a8a7-4f7e-8d13-c651813aa1c7">
<p local-id=3D"6396f0f1-5651-4e37-a857-5e769f71d514">Make sure you used <co=
de>--force</code> when signing</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"701be77f-73b1-4b1b-88d0-5d745d0d4785"><strong>If it works lo=
cally, you're ready for the next step!</strong></p>
<hr local-id=3D"5a142a2e-f11c-4262-90de-8c7a296c84cf">
<h2 local-id=3D"16a54072-fadd-4527-89fd-089064028b08" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-=F0=9F=93=A6Part5:CreatingaDMG(=F0=9F=94=84EVERYBUILD)"=
>=F0=9F=93=A6 Part 5: Creating a DMG (=F0=9F=94=84 EVERY BUILD)</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"5c39db67-c635-4138-a6ee-c481bba0eae5" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step11:WhyPackageasDMG?">Step 11: Why Package as DMG?</=
h3>
<p local-id=3D"0ae87a43-6fd7-44e7-a548-19a69efa5229"><strong>DMG Benefits:<=
/strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"f4fbf1ca-11c5-43fb-b45c-34f551cd72a8">
<li local-id=3D"896890f3-700c-408e-90a0-69e90c12c00a">
<p local-id=3D"6c56ea9a-3d11-4a7a-92bc-5e684a28eba1">Professional distribut=
ion format</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6c2b4c8a-c859-46c1-8308-efcb0f5dc288">
<p local-id=3D"f4ee83d7-9592-42d9-a6e4-f0f8282071e3">Can include custom bac=
kground, icons, license</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7976093d-9833-469c-8de7-2fa2f9189c50">
<p local-id=3D"eec60ae8-0b2e-4d56-a148-f7a09e8cf3a0">Single file to distrib=
ute</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"51f3d2e9-d462-430d-bc61-2fe8acf45c9c">
<p local-id=3D"8a21adfa-9375-4fda-b5a7-766b21fa346b">DMGs can be notarized =
and stapled (raw binaries cannot!)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"bb166e98-1eae-4047-b3ce-c7113da7aa10">
<p local-id=3D"9e8fb765-fd69-443e-aa56-cbeab6fa00b9">Provides a consistent =
download experience</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"018669f2-c333-48bd-a94b-48917252e0ba"><strong>Important:</st=
rong> Raw Mach-O executables (like your binary) <strong>cannot be stapled</=
strong>. Only <code>.app</code> bundles, <code>.dmg</code> files, and <code=
>.pkg</code> installers support stapling. This is why we package in a DMG.<=
/p>
<h3 local-id=3D"66e673dc-b3e0-4ee2-8411-245d95566517" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step12:CreateaDMGwithYourSignedBinary">Step 12: Create =
a DMG with Your Signed Binary</h3>
<p local-id=3D"4080e54c-23dd-4fe9-9c6b-1836222d7c53"><strong>Create a tempo=
rary folder for DMG contents:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">cd /Use=
rs/joaquinaraujo/github/bzm-mcp/dist

# Create temp directory
mkdir -p ~/tmp/bzm-mcp-dmg

# Copy the SIGNED binary into it
cp bzm-mcp-macos-arm64 ~/tmp/bzm-mcp-dmg/</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"cafc1ee1-5bd5-4ce5-9c5a-c21325d85eb5"><strong>Create the DMG=
:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">hdiutil=
 create -volname "BlazeMeter MCP" \
  -srcfolder ~/tmp/bzm-mcp-dmg \
  -ov -format UDZO \
  bzm-mcp-macos-arm64.dmg

# Clean up temp directory
rm -rf ~/tmp/bzm-mcp-dmg</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"eec7d929-30f5-455c-aeca-79eec7fbafd2"><strong>Breaking down =
the command:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"5c508734-41fa-4ceb-86ce-2de84e752b6b">
<li local-id=3D"cb224089-a534-4992-b0cb-37ed614c2556">
<p local-id=3D"7dd433a3-9bf4-4757-930e-cdd08ff61a93"><code>-volname</code> =
- Name shown when DMG is mounted (users see this)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"139a8a5f-6a38-4fec-b8d9-b7a03e6b9e04">
<p local-id=3D"5eb20368-82d8-454c-b1ce-c67392a9ad2e"><code>-srcfolder</code=
> - What to put in the DMG (your signed binary!)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"54dce468-ead3-4bdc-9d7f-b56a2345027a">
<p local-id=3D"1b5afa77-5b4c-4231-a334-2a52159b8c9b"><code>-ov</code> - Ove=
rwrite if DMG already exists</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"012dfe39-174e-4ed2-a8e7-5d292f012049">
<p local-id=3D"9a561ff5-3c44-4834-8fc9-0bdbc1244645"><code>-format UDZO</co=
de> - Compressed format (smaller file size)</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"a46644b7-71ce-41c0-8158-12e9188f41f4" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step13:SigntheDMG">Step 13: Sign the DMG</h3>
<p local-id=3D"2f098d42-63a5-44c6-b3db-116a38a9f871"><strong>Sign the DMG c=
ontainer itself:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">codesig=
n --sign "Developer ID Application: Your Name (TEAM_ID)" \
  --timestamp \
  --force \
  --verbose \
  bzm-mcp-macos-arm64.dmg</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"03686ead-75ff-41a2-9158-861d33f73afa"><strong>Why sign the D=
MG?</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"c0c08d0b-875b-4b10-ac87-1fbba6216d6e">
<li local-id=3D"3eb933e1-7098-476b-b034-b5c72e7c7f68">
<p local-id=3D"c9471c23-970f-4754-b373-7af18076d29e">Protects the DMG conta=
iner from tampering</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8545b5a4-93ba-4853-a79d-38a66f36513f">
<p local-id=3D"420ae64e-dbb3-45f5-bcd1-2d7cccbd327e">Required for notarizat=
ion</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"401c3e89-42fb-4a0a-a552-9ef11727e2b2">
<p local-id=3D"6fde00d7-633b-447e-92b5-4ccbb044ee5b">Provides an additional=
 layer of security</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"d8b1e48a-d7f6-4d36-92b3-c210e9a24ae1"><strong>Verify DMG sig=
nature:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">codesig=
n --verify --verbose bzm-mcp-macos-arm64.dmg</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"e8c8cef9-b692-42d7-84b3-e156d8bf134d"><strong>Expected outpu=
t:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">bzm-mcp=
-macos-arm64.dmg: valid on disk
bzm-mcp-macos-arm64.dmg: satisfies its Designated Requirement</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr local-id=3D"ddcbb37f-ba34-4172-a40b-fcf277b8bd71">
<h2 local-id=3D"c86d23c2-28bf-4f29-863d-829b828f4d03" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-=F0=9F=93=A6Part5B:CreatingaZIPArchive(Alternative-Curr=
entMethod)">=F0=9F=93=A6 Part 5B: Creating a ZIP Archive (Alternative - Cur=
rent Method)</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"ad65fcd8-94f4-4048-8ab8-7c8786efa17e" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step11B:WhyUseZIPInsteadofDMG?">Step 11B: Why Use ZIP I=
nstead of DMG?</h3>
<p local-id=3D"85e20808-7265-4a83-8a85-6f4dae8dad56"><strong>ZIP Benefits:<=
/strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"d62421f5-893d-4eba-a0da-2e21e46f4957">
<li local-id=3D"dc788724-9e05-4fd7-bbad-1ddd4f32a083">
<p local-id=3D"58731596-46cf-4341-8bec-fa393e8f0a14">Simpler creation proce=
ss (no signing of the archive itself needed)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"668f05c4-a3d7-48e7-823a-e571a9d78efc">
<p local-id=3D"bcc9dd4e-40ba-4f8e-9e29-0b4f5ba9a650">Standard format univer=
sally supported</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"00d4b567-3bd0-467d-8ca2-b6f1417a0bfb">
<p local-id=3D"cf22839c-589a-4390-83f4-ba9bda4a7b47">Faster to create and p=
rocess</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"23806417-387c-4455-83d5-d9f5e5ada23a">
<p local-id=3D"2713cfa1-6e5a-4c58-9e51-0cdbcc711cdc">Direct notarization of=
 the ZIP file</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"4bc82cf3-ea80-4dc5-9d6d-c7ae0b6df44d"><strong>ZIP Limitation=
s:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"21ca18e7-0b6e-4a75-8811-a004a9d07e46">
<li local-id=3D"bf8d311f-53b1-476b-a95b-f653637592cd">
<p local-id=3D"2e592f25-ee84-4fd0-954d-b1e99668c062">=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F <st=
rong>Cannot be stapled</strong> - Unlike DMG, ZIP files don't support stapl=
ing the notarization ticket</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"919107ac-5aa9-4004-b333-b88107e4240f">
<p local-id=3D"5f3d6924-268c-4c3b-8272-3d0c856570bb">First-run verification=
 requires internet connection (macOS checks online)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a347a3b0-293b-4993-8d6b-53cd32043939">
<p local-id=3D"edca8803-9731-4b56-b208-4a5ed4d712e7">Less polished user exp=
erience compared to custom DMG</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"8c0c4ca4-f1c4-4976-bde2-f1aa2a56f449"><strong>When to use ZI=
P vs DMG:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"4b91c5cf-b29b-4e92-9fdc-12aed5c0a7f8">
<li local-id=3D"b44d2729-2f59-4b66-8871-e1bf09d9600c">
<p local-id=3D"ec7cc052-7b3a-47fd-8c5c-8cceb953b88b"><strong>Use ZIP</stron=
g> - For command-line tools, internal distribution, or when simplicity is p=
referred</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"07eefb31-f633-4d3d-89f7-425e480e85b3">
<p local-id=3D"8b41de06-3835-4f9b-84ec-961c63aea1b5"><strong>Use DMG</stron=
g> - For end-user applications requiring offline verification and a polishe=
d installer experience</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"fb32f7c0-e93f-4fc8-af2b-4debcbb68ceb"><strong>Important:</st=
rong> While ZIP files cannot be stapled, the notarized binary inside is sti=
ll recorded by Apple. macOS will verify it online on first run (requires in=
ternet connection).</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"04ab2189-123c-4cff-8353-6fd606bdac4e" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step12B:CreateaZIPArchivewithYourSignedBinary">Step 12B=
: Create a ZIP Archive with Your Signed Binary</h3>
<p local-id=3D"20cbb4f0-ef5c-482f-85f0-5423af37ee59"><strong>Create a ZIP u=
sing ditto (preserves macOS metadata):</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">cd /Use=
rs/joaquinaraujo/github/bzm-mcp/dist

# Create ZIP archive preserving resource forks and metadata
ditto -c -k --sequesterRsrc --keepParent bzm-mcp-macos-arm64 bzm-mcp-macos-=
arm64.zip</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"590a3a16-8a3d-47ca-b089-dc9535b897e1"><strong>Breaking down =
the command:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"b016bf41-702c-4926-8362-17081e9e91e6">
<li local-id=3D"7f25aa7b-776b-4d39-9251-283bab368a64">
<p local-id=3D"0e8a4aaa-269a-4c42-b6da-32ef3b88731b"><code>-c</code> - Crea=
te an archive</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ad3d7663-354d-41e6-b089-56882fa509d9">
<p local-id=3D"34813e11-8caa-4ad7-af67-060e57861ff0"><code>-k</code> - Crea=
te a PKZip archive (standard ZIP format)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3312ce3b-659b-4804-a77f-47f3b5e0987a">
<p local-id=3D"6c516b56-1985-44a9-8507-84d58e1e9fa5"><code>--sequesterRsrc<=
/code> - Preserve resource forks and HFS+ metadata in AppleDouble format</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"1c7e1889-f363-4d2c-830d-e00dcd6acd33">
<p local-id=3D"5455501f-6822-4958-847f-ab440286a373"><code>--keepParent</co=
de> - Include the parent directory name (so extraction creates a folder)</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"9b5e862c-63cf-46fb-aaf4-0d94bcb156d7">
<p local-id=3D"b5e011ce-4fe5-4f4b-9e4b-d0453f8c0f52">Source: <code>bzm-mcp-=
macos-arm64</code> (your signed binary!)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"939d8168-c9d9-4db6-9f33-65bf07e9f4f6">
<p local-id=3D"165fc67c-b93e-4f25-b45d-635c838be93d">Destination: <code>bzm=
-mcp-macos-arm64.zip</code></p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"bdc49995-e267-4df5-9f4f-b85d0bdc0f4e"><strong>Why use </stro=
ng><code>ditto</code> instead of regular <code>zip</code>?</p>
<ul local-id=3D"44f370d2-fc0c-457e-8ad8-70e48a5ebfc7">
<li local-id=3D"a2551212-cf89-4613-8191-eb750f9e68d1">
<p local-id=3D"7110c1e1-6537-4512-a81d-4daa255b74ba">Properly preserves mac=
OS extended attributes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7a8e6473-f6ce-4012-8d1b-fa68fd35a55b">
<p local-id=3D"6dded09c-a281-4672-83ac-ca0a0d10daff">Maintains code signatu=
res correctly</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b9c29af0-1afd-47cf-8485-31b5bd086b73">
<p local-id=3D"d74a069e-aa66-4f9c-8680-83f278449ca6">Apple-recommended tool=
 for creating archives</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"77c21839-0b00-4247-a37c-064cbe05b198">
<p local-id=3D"31ee5181-1462-4ad7-8f3a-b9fa3d2ea93f">Better handling of res=
ource forks and metadata</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"c1776550-7d2a-4e78-b9c4-bef0ee9b1322"><strong>Important Note=
s:</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"c22bee14-34d3-4002-8c57-92b4fd52194f">
<li local-id=3D"dfe31739-ddff-43eb-9750-141b09294d61">
<p local-id=3D"ceeb2b60-f380-47d2-8f54-cec8907d9531">The binary inside MUST=
 already be signed before creating the ZIP</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"215ed03a-6ccf-4f14-9ab6-ad7be8e95bfb">
<p local-id=3D"25370a96-0295-42a4-a253-f8b8119b8f48">ZIP files do NOT need =
to be signed separately (unlike DMG)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"388c3aa7-cc1a-4a33-8723-7790f40afd78">
<p local-id=3D"eabd9f3a-d1f5-4d93-b1ee-7ca2dc4ce07e">You will notarize the =
ZIP itself in the next step</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"09e32bb3-06cf-4388-b591-923bdf8d2110">
<p local-id=3D"df49f327-90ca-41a6-a087-ee5added408e">You CANNOT staple the =
ZIP (only DMG/app/pkg support stapling)</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"17526c72-8689-4b02-a9ef-294f34159fb4" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step13B:VerifyZIPContents">Step 13B: Verify ZIP Content=
s</h3>
<p local-id=3D"ae5f4215-8b93-460f-8618-b4dddc8957b8"><strong>Extract and ve=
rify the binary is properly signed:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Creat=
e temp directory to test extraction
mkdir -p ~/tmp/zip-test
cd ~/tmp/zip-test

# Extract the ZIP
unzip /Users/joaquinaraujo/github/bzm-mcp/dist/bzm-mcp-macos-arm64.zip

# Verify the extracted binary signature
codesign --display --verbose=3D4 bzm-mcp-macos-arm64

# Should show: Authority=3DDeveloper ID Application: ...

# Clean up
cd ~
rm -rf ~/tmp/zip-test</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"db942ff3-ab16-4f5c-95c7-999b7cb5f2f9"><strong>What to look f=
or:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"8a0c9d6a-7948-4dd3-a880-7672e6b9c69b">
<li local-id=3D"867dda7a-c7bf-4ccf-9643-9e5c0c9f34d2">
<p local-id=3D"325dd4fc-7425-40fa-a0ec-a1f49ee11f7e">=E2=9C=85 Binary extra=
cts successfully</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d243e9a5-614a-44d4-a509-c994c510e9a6">
<p local-id=3D"29982132-ac2d-4f86-b73c-9021f38080ef">=E2=9C=85 Code signatu=
re is intact (<code>Authority=3DDeveloper ID Application</code>)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e77b23f8-5f23-4f7d-b4db-fdec9b89b2e6">
<p local-id=3D"61ef1b73-fdc6-4889-80c0-79aab9a916f8">=E2=9C=85 Entitlements=
 are preserved</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"da4a5dbd-ef8e-417e-8739-d9d822c77824">
<p local-id=3D"e73154e7-a9d9-4672-bc78-bcbbf05b5222">=E2=9D=8C If signature=
 shows <code>adhoc</code>, the ZIP was created from unsigned binary</p></li=
>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"9918c123-c37e-42e5-8e5c-e62c223d3da1"><strong>If signature i=
s missing or adhoc:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"d8bad3dc-7759-42f9-bbdc-0add15b6d741">
<li local-id=3D"5bf3e5e8-05a4-41d2-a803-6140af6f654f">
<p local-id=3D"838b2581-d4bd-4eb2-9894-59b82f8b2879">Delete the ZIP file</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"44f18aae-9723-4c17-b1cd-b2af4e7424bb">
<p local-id=3D"fd588aa0-c8a9-4fd4-ae49-f3574631d800">Re-sign the binary pro=
perly</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"65f0cc6a-9020-4dd1-9c5c-7ccef5ded5aa">
<p local-id=3D"7b4ffa78-8f60-4159-b07c-5d44016ea83d">Create a new ZIP from =
the signed binary</p></li>
</ul>
<hr local-id=3D"fbfb5ce4-a003-4226-bd9d-ad7502534ed0">
<h2 local-id=3D"59c97a0c-4af4-4291-a906-0f5c19526b4f" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-=E2=9C=85Part6:Notarization">=E2=9C=85 Part 6: Notariza=
tion</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"1b5191e2-6c05-408a-b1ff-03d881923d88" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step14:UnderstandingNotarization">Step 14: Understandin=
g Notarization</h3>
<p local-id=3D"24747f44-b4dc-4a37-9a74-9df459c3288c"><strong>What it is:</s=
trong> You upload your signed DMG to Apple's servers. They automatically sc=
an it for malware and policy violations. If it passes, they return a "ticke=
t" that says "Apple has checked this."</p>
<p local-id=3D"0407777d-b1f3-4542-8281-b9441216d848"><strong>What Apple che=
cks:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"169dfe1e-4445-4231-995d-1b6c361d3707">
<li local-id=3D"2d3aadf3-91c7-4a83-a8c0-855e5168e0a6">
<p local-id=3D"1efb2e45-7fb9-4b95-8dbb-792f9207d9af">The DMG is properly si=
gned</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"790e9628-c2b0-47a2-99a1-cf5bafde5001">
<p local-id=3D"b36c9c07-e877-49a0-a410-5847bb564590">The binary inside the =
DMG is properly signed</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"33062c69-896e-47bb-95ea-17b769fae3fd">
<p local-id=3D"3fb322bd-b669-426c-a900-148b6a8e066c">No known malware signa=
tures</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5c5e7893-13ce-4718-9539-0ab674a73364">
<p local-id=3D"2a6e4f84-0f43-48d9-a9fb-77492ef4435b">Hardened runtime is en=
abled</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2e1ff507-7749-4ab0-bae1-94c737f11362">
<p local-id=3D"1e062e12-e41a-4422-89dd-ce4a29cd4f65">No suspicious code pat=
terns</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"d8a88879-5873-46f0-95f4-475ec3fead82"><strong>Important:</st=
rong> Notarization is NOT the same as App Store review. It's automated and =
takes 1-5 minutes.</p>
<p local-id=3D"eb80d7cc-533d-4c21-a7c1-bc1f413820d6"><strong>For raw binari=
es:</strong> When you notarize a DMG, Apple records the cryptographic hash =
of the binary inside. When a user extracts and runs the binary, macOS check=
s online (first run only) to verify it came from a notarized package.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"5abb4618-85b8-461d-8da5-9121fea3502b" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step15:StoreYourCredentials(=E2=8F=B0ONE-TIMESETUP)">St=
ep 15: Store Your Credentials (=E2=8F=B0 ONE-TIME SETUP)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"91436919-9a96-4f21-b930-c940d820ae5f"><strong>Set up your AP=
I key for notarization:</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"47a9432e-1a21-49c2-a031-275bfcd6d25d">First, find your Key I=
D (it's in the filename of your .p8 file):</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># List =
your API key to get the Key ID
ls -la ~/.apple-keys/
# If your file is AuthKey_ABC123XYZ.p8
# Then ABC123XYZ is your Key ID</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"c291023f-2c6a-423f-8b63-1960fc7b1627"><strong>Store credenti=
als in Keychain (this is secure and recommended):</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">xcrun n=
otarytool store-credentials "bzm-mcp-notary" \
  --key ~/.apple-keys/AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8 \
  --key-id XXXXXXXXXX \
  --issuer YOUR-ISSUER-UUID</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"bbe7de20-b953-422a-b655-9452d7bd7545"><strong>Breaking it do=
wn:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"fa15ea83-cef8-4469-b3b0-b62d076149e5">
<li local-id=3D"f8e6815f-e997-4f93-b2b5-5b2d7c2c1d1e">
<p local-id=3D"c005f46e-868a-4e9b-9ae7-493c450dc7f4"><code>"bzm-mcp-notary"=
</code> - A profile name you choose (anything memorable)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"82937321-cccc-4758-a6fc-b2c9cfe4117f">
<p local-id=3D"ca4aee4c-9c8c-4035-acbb-cad7b19c2124"><code>--key</code> - P=
ath to your .p8 API key file in <code>~/.apple-keys/</code></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"59ea4352-8661-47e2-a238-623f7c9332f1">
<p local-id=3D"ba61f63a-4d6f-4477-9f87-19786762b93a"><code>--key-id</code> =
- The ID from the filename (the XXXXXXXXXX part)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6384aa69-77da-48e0-a42a-0962755e4b76">
<p local-id=3D"0d844bd6-4825-42d0-8244-6f84911ea698"><code>--issuer</code> =
- Your Apple Issuer UUID</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"add5bee4-907b-4853-8b03-95b7d24771c1"><strong>What this does=
:</strong> Saves credentials securely in your Keychain so you don't have to=
 type them each time.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e5a1fbc0-2bab-4375-a429-371214012abf"><strong>Security Note:=
</strong> The <code>.p8</code> file will remain in <code>~/.apple-keys/</co=
de> as it's needed for future signing operations. This directory has restri=
cted permissions (only you can access), and the credentials are also stored=
 encrypted in your Keychain via the notarytool profile.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2ad9c08a-95b8-4e80-a472-845cb45c3ac3"><strong>You only need =
to do this once</strong> - the credentials are saved for future notarizatio=
ns.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"e7cf2fd1-bd62-4f8b-9007-f517e0ae25de" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step16:SubmitforNotarization(=F0=9F=94=84EVERYBUILD)">S=
tep 16: Submit for Notarization (=F0=9F=94=84 EVERY BUILD)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"13f9b8c6-0efd-47ef-8a18-bce3271652fb"><strong>For ZIP files =
(Current Method):</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">xcrun n=
otarytool submit bzm-mcp-macos-arm64.zip \
  --keychain-profile "bzm-mcp-notary" \
  --wait</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"fdbe8737-ba88-4d9c-aa55-eaab54bb95ea"><strong>For DMG files =
(Alternative Method):</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">xcrun n=
otarytool submit bzm-mcp-macos-arm64.dmg \
  --keychain-profile "bzm-mcp-notary" \
  --wait</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"94a7e817-6d0a-4473-bf10-f868a0419e9c"><strong>Breaking it do=
wn:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"b45906a6-08cf-41f4-8e2a-d924a7c32b49">
<li local-id=3D"17ed0a0c-0a6c-4a0c-b88c-00059bd8d2fc">
<p local-id=3D"19237db8-b173-41f2-9e17-155db3b0c81c"><code>submit</code> - =
Upload to Apple (works for ZIP, DMG, PKG, APP)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3c1d9390-a0cc-468b-a246-cdfc879b53cf">
<p local-id=3D"88275fa5-ecaf-4b9d-b8ce-da3d395c6bb8"><code>--keychain-profi=
le</code> - Use the credentials you stored</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f800c1b0-fecc-4052-9f8f-eda5cd7d32a7">
<p local-id=3D"c67af855-9cf4-4bc4-a045-49cce63646f9"><code>--wait</code> - =
Don't return until done (could take 1-5 minutes)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"f03da9c3-e947-4e7b-9160-b3137dd6e334"><strong>What you'll se=
e:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Submitt=
ing bzm-mcp-macos-arm64.zip for notarization...
Successfully uploaded file
  id: a1b2c3d4-1234-5678-9abc-def012345678
  path: /path/to/bzm-mcp-macos-arm64.zip

Waiting for processing to complete...
Current status: In Progress.....
Current status: Accepted

Processing complete
  id: a1b2c3d4-1234-5678-9abc-def012345678
  status: Accepted</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"8cc7d98c-0822-486c-b4fc-968081447857"><strong>If it gets rej=
ected:</strong> Check the logs:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">xcrun n=
otarytool log a1b2c3d4-1234-5678-9abc-def012345678 \
  --keychain-profile "bzm-mcp-notary"</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"5ab27645-25f6-4783-8843-35cff602aeab"><strong>Common rejecti=
on reasons:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"69dd0b5f-e0c2-4510-a409-85db4692b17c">
<li local-id=3D"30a79572-e7d8-4859-83f5-efc691bfaa65">
<p local-id=3D"1aae7b54-c3ad-4825-8a26-5070720c2e70">Binary inside package =
not properly signed</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"bb7b14f0-499a-46e8-9140-afd9be4f9cac">
<p local-id=3D"1223b1f4-17d4-4ede-9abb-41d4d5dae076">Missing hardened runti=
me</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cd44c96b-5c87-43bf-8647-be74d9acf7fb">
<p local-id=3D"0b92fff4-6fe6-4d9c-a712-932e8c4db41f">Missing entitlements f=
or PyInstaller apps</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"66822909-6570-4fdc-a760-ece8387e0b83">
<p local-id=3D"d6b72870-c2b0-44f9-875c-f8e3544a6820">Signature issues with =
embedded frameworks</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"27af5087-61c4-4a5c-9850-b0388c3e831c" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step17:CheckNotarizationHistory(Optional)">Step 17: Che=
ck Notarization History (Optional)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"cf539f7c-656c-4a1c-b90d-4016bf2a13d9"><strong>See all your s=
ubmissions:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">xcrun n=
otarytool history \
  --keychain-profile "bzm-mcp-notary"</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr local-id=3D"6f89d7e7-0cf6-49fc-a22b-aa9630a660fc">
<h2 local-id=3D"1a354aaf-f79b-488d-a2de-4121d65bdfd9" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-=F0=9F=8E=ABPart7:Stapling(=F0=9F=94=84EVERYBUILD-DMGON=
LY)">=F0=9F=8E=AB Part 7: Stapling (=F0=9F=94=84 EVERY BUILD - DMG ONLY)</h=
2>
<h3 local-id=3D"22c87518-9928-4cfa-b3f9-5a74e07a611e" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step18:UnderstandingStapling">Step 18: Understanding St=
apling</h3>
<p local-id=3D"62ca1b34-e5cc-4db2-aaa7-541632775295"><strong>=E2=9A=A0=EF=
=B8=8F IMPORTANT: This step only applies to DMG files. ZIP files cannot be =
stapled!</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"dd27168d-3240-4cc2-9870-06abae64ab86"><strong>The problem:</=
strong> Even though Apple approved your package, the approval "ticket" live=
s on Apple's servers. If a user is offline during first run, macOS can't ve=
rify it.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e50c323a-628c-4e2a-a130-896e3810c26a"><strong>The solution (=
DMG only):</strong> "Staple" the notarization ticket directly to your DMG. =
This embeds Apple's approval into the file itself.</p>
<p local-id=3D"231f5f5f-44b9-41b5-92ed-9404a31b9bf5"><strong>What can be st=
apled:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"a0c9dd28-868b-4b1e-9c36-832b559bff5a">
<li local-id=3D"c0b369b0-a792-4aab-9fb9-7434e6e2c5ac">
<p local-id=3D"ea5b2b1b-bc68-486d-95e7-34c54831068c">=E2=9C=85 <code>.dmg</=
code> files (disk images)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2b16297b-ebc5-4294-bda7-211728058301">
<p local-id=3D"e144a86b-5870-48d6-a8b3-9f69a07058d5">=E2=9C=85 <code>.app</=
code> bundles (applications)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3e27fecd-04f9-4e71-ad1e-64afc608a785">
<p local-id=3D"afc3c9ff-0105-4bd8-9fbd-8f9223034647">=E2=9C=85 <code>.pkg</=
code> files (installers)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8c8479d1-4423-4a8c-a038-50178f40d683">
<p local-id=3D"f30d417b-2bdf-40a2-863d-da26817fa7b2">=E2=9D=8C <code>.zip</=
code> files (not supported!)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"dd8c9bcb-6bb8-43ac-a5d9-029f4ed40c0b">
<p local-id=3D"c2783074-7342-4e84-9043-0723311616a6">=E2=9D=8C Raw Mach-O e=
xecutables (like your standalone binary)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"eea5bbdd-8310-464f-9ef1-5109dbcc575e"><strong>Why you can't =
staple ZIP files:</strong><br>
The stapler tool requires a file format that supports extended attributes i=
n a way that ZIP doesn't support. ZIP files store metadata differently and =
don't support Apple's stapling mechanism.</p>
<p local-id=3D"64c22c91-b079-45bf-ba43-c970fcdecc3c"><strong>Impact of not =
stapling (ZIP files):</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"85c77d98-c926-47ca-891d-dbde0868991d">
<li local-id=3D"18d4bf0f-c67d-4da5-a937-b4bcf1603b47">
<p local-id=3D"07fd586e-a475-4004-9a37-b8b6eefd658d"><strong>ZIP (no stapli=
ng possible):</strong> macOS checks online on first run (requires internet =
connection)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2e12679e-d703-41d7-8897-be1b005d3d83">
<p local-id=3D"fff95ab2-4316-486d-be2e-7029da6d8e42"><strong>DMG with stapl=
ing:</strong> macOS verifies offline (works without internet)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"22e0e425-97ec-4695-943e-1ddfad34f2a4">
<p local-id=3D"8568e010-ef2b-4d17-b549-1005331e3bd0">Both methods provide s=
ecurity, but DMG offers better offline experience</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"16d11d31-fd7b-42e2-830e-3d463779c38c"><strong>How notarizati=
on protects ZIP contents:</strong><br>
When Apple notarizes your ZIP, they record the hash of every file inside it=
, including your binary. Even without stapling:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"a1dc96ce-97f2-45b6-bdb2-fc6ec3107b40">
<li local-id=3D"2f18cc9c-fc26-49ca-8bda-ad22b7303959">
<p local-id=3D"1b0d769d-46a8-4ec5-b432-e3f6422a91b8">The binary is recorded=
 in Apple's notarization database</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2cfb4e74-3214-45d1-b6c9-7d711b0b6852">
<p local-id=3D"b4d8b509-a813-4624-b660-4e07771b5617">macOS checks online du=
ring first run (caches result for subsequent runs)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1cf9bf25-d9c2-4ee0-bc9e-e220a5cd3635">
<p local-id=3D"a8aab973-fee9-4fcd-9586-31778fa5ed24">The binary is just as =
secure, but requires internet for first verification</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"93f1dccf-d518-4222-93a1-d24a65594a4e" id=3D"MCPMacOsSigning=
-Notarization-Stamp-Step19:StapletheNotarizationTicket(DMGOnly)">Step 19: S=
taple the Notarization Ticket (DMG Only)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"25b60d91-e652-4cd9-9bc5-934a29b6c904"><strong>=E2=9A=A0=EF=
=B8=8F Skip this step if using ZIP files - proceed to Part 8 (Testing)</str=
ong></p>
